@Naros thanks. i get the dual management worry but honestly the current behaviour is worse than anything misalignment could do. right now the decoder just binds by position against the full table, so with a column list publication the values land on the wrong columns. if the types happen to line up you dont even get an error, just wrong data sitting in the right shape. a null or a schema failure would at least tell you something is off.

and i dont think users should have to keep column.include.list in sync with the publication at all. postgres already knows what the publication covers. the relation message carries the exact published columns during streaming, the problem is only that the snapshot refresh overwrites that model with the full table read over jdbc. so either dont overwrite it, or read the column list from pg_publication_tables.attnames when refreshing. the sql server connector already does it this way btw, DBZ-2495 builds the model from the capture instance columns instead of the full table.

auto managed publications shouldnt be affected since debezium never creates them with column lists anyway. the divergence can only happen when someone hand manages the publication, and in that case the catalog is right there to read.

@jpechane on it, will open the pr. and yes will add that check, if both connector level filtering and a publication column list are set the connector fails at startup and says which side to drop.
